This repository is a DERIVATIVE WORK of CircleMUD, which is itself a
derivative work of DikuMUD.  That is true of every part of it: the C server
under reference/, the Go port at the root, the tooling, the documentation,
and the game data under data/.

Copyright in the material written for Disgracelands - the original
2001-2008 server and this revival, including the Go port, which contains
none of CircleMUD's C code - is held by Dave O'Connor.  That copyright
does not and cannot grant anyone terms more permissive than the licenses
this work derives from.  The CircleMUD license and the DikuMUD license,
both reproduced verbatim below, govern this work in its entirety, and no
part of it may be used except in compliance with them.

In particular, and without narrowing anything below:

-- NON-COMMERCIAL.  This work must not be used to make money or to obtain
   compensation of any kind.  No fees to play, no donations, no paid
   perks, no reimbursement of hosting or hardware costs, no selling copies
   or charging for distribution.

-- CREDIT.  data/text/credits must be preserved as it stands (additions
   are allowed; removals and edits are not) and must be displayed by the
   `credits` command.  The `CIRCLEMUD` help entry must stay intact and be
   shown in full by `help circlemud`.  The login sequence - everything a
   player sees between connecting and playing - must name the DikuMUD and
   CircleMUD creators; that is data/text/greetings, and it must be sent on
   every transport, with no client-side splash screen substituted for it.

-- SHIP THIS FILE.  This license must accompany any copy or portion of
   this work, including works derived from it, AS IS.

-- KEEP THE NOTICES.  Notices of copyright, licensing or authorship must
   not be removed, changed or modified in any source file - CircleMUD's,
   DikuMUD's, a third-party patch author's, or this project's.

-- A REWRITE IS NOT AN EXEMPTION.  The Go port reimplements CircleMUD's
   mechanics, file formats and world data in a different language; it is a
   derivative work all the same, and the CircleMUD license addresses the
   "our MUD is totally rewritten" claim explicitly (see below).

Authorship, for the credit requirement:

